[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   TEP-9 step 097 -- Voyager PWS plasma-frequency channel
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   The PWS VLISM electron-density collections (PDS4 bundle
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   urn:nasa:pds:voyager-pws-vlism-density) record per-event electron
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   plasma frequency f_pe, the derived density N_e = 4 pi^2 m_e eps0
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   f_pe^2 / e^2 with min/max bounds, and the spacecraft state vector --
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   the only in-situ measurement series across a candidate boundary in
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   the outer heliosphere.
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   Two questions are addressed, with care taken not to conflate the
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   measurement channels:
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   1. Is the measured structure plasma or lapse artifact?  The measured
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   f_pe is referenced to the onboard frequency scale; under a
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   conformal lapse every onboard-referenced frequency shifts by the
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   same factor, so a lapse offset cannot selectively move f_pe (and
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   the SCLK channel already bounds the onboard-vs-ground rate ratio
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   at ~5e-5).  A *constants-shift* reading is different: if e_eff,
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   m_e,eff or eps0,eff scale with A(phi) while N_e stays smooth,
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   measured f_pe could mimic density structure.  The step computes
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   the combined constants-shift deltaX = 2 delta ln f_pe required to
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   attribute each observed jump to such a shift at constant density,
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   and compares it with the ~1e-2 lapse contrast implied by the
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   comet channel.  If the required deltaX is orders of magnitude
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   larger, the structure is confirmed as real plasma structure --
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   which is what a plasma-coupled screening transition would *use*
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   (co-location, not illusion).
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   2. What does the residual (smooth-segment) channel bound?  Within
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   inter-jump segments the f_pe drift is slow; the segment-to-
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   segment consistency and the step sizes versus the 18-Hz spectrum
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   analyser channel width bound any residual constants-shift along
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   the trajectory at the few-percent level -- a bound that applies
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   to a lapse gradient threading V1's path specifically.
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   Also reported: per-event separation of the spacecraft position and
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   velocity directions from the TNO axis and anti-axis (both spacecraft
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   sample the anti-axis hemisphere / mirror-cap region), and the
[2026-09-21 15:11:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 097]   measured density-gradient scale as a candidate screening length.
